  <Instrument_Host>
    <name>Vega 1 Spacecraft</name>
    <type>Spacecraft</type>
    <naif_host_id>-66</naif_host_id>
    <description>The Soviet Vega program spacecraft were based on the earlier Venera program spacecraft, and carried balloon probes and surface landers identical to the earlier Venera spacecraft for deployment to Venus. After releasing its probe and lander at Venus in June 1985, Vega 1 used a Venus gravity assist to continue on to join the armada at comet 1P/Halley. Image data returned by Vega 1 in March of 1986 contributed to the successful flyby planning for the Giotto spacecraft. Vega 1 survived its encounter with the comet, despite multiple dust collisions, returning data from a distance of about 8889km from the nucleus. The spacecraft is now in a heliocentric orbit with a period of about 281 days.</description>
